MID_EV13_039_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_039_m01_001: Pardon me, Queen Theodora. I come with a message\nfrom the Divine Sovereign.
MID_EV13_039_m01_002: It has been some time since we heard from you.\nI pray the Divine Sovereign is well.
MID_EV13_039_m01_003: He says you've shown great valor in the qualifiers\nand commends you on advancing to the main bouts.
MID_EV13_039_m01_004: He looks forward to your continued success in the\ntournament proper.
MID_EV13_039_m01_005: It begins in Seftim. He hopes you will make the most\nof your time until then.
MID_EV13_039_m01_006: Very well. Inform the Divine Sovereign that we\nunderstand.
MID_EV13_039_m01_007: He was slightly concerned that you might grow bored\nwith so much downtime, Queen Theodora.
MID_EV13_039_m01_008: If you'd like, I'd be glad to show you some popular\nentertainment spots here in Dagsion.
MID_EV13_039_m01_009: No need. I plan to put this precious time to use.
MID_EV13_039_m01_010: Boss, did I hear her right that the main event isn't\nuntil Seftim?
MID_EV13_039_m01_011: That would give us three entire months until our\nnext match.
MID_EV13_039_m01_012: I see we find ourselves with time on our hands.
MID_EV13_039_m01_013: Yeah, but I don't get paid for downtime. How am I\ngonna make money with no work to do?
MID_EV13_039_m01_014: Are we only gonna get our base salary during those\nthree months? Don't love that.
MID_EV13_039_m01_015: <NCA>Consider returning to Megaira.
MID_EV13_039_m01_016: <NCB>Consider ways to use the time.
MID_EV13_039_m01_017: <ACA>With three months to ourselves, we have the option\nof returning to Megaira.
MID_EV13_039_m01_018: <ACA>I would like to visit my father's grave to tell him his\nmurderer has been slain.
MID_EV13_039_m01_019: <ACB>We must put this unexpected time to good use.\nDo any of you have ideas?
MID_EV13_039_m01_020: I've been thinking hard, boss.
MID_EV13_039_m01_021: You said that amulet Troy gave you broke when\nyou were using Mahadu's arm, right?
MID_EV13_039_m01_022: And ever since then, things have been bad with\nyou hearing voices and all.
MID_EV13_039_m01_023: So let's go visit Troy and get a new one!
MID_EV13_039_m01_024: That is a fine idea.
MID_EV13_039_m01_025: Even if she does not have a replacement, she can\ntell us where the original was found.
MID_EV13_039_m01_026: Thank you, Tobias. I never even considered it.
MID_EV13_039_m01_027: When one feels as cornered as I have been, it is\nhard to see the simple way out.
MID_EV13_039_m01_028: We have time enough for a trip, so I've no concerns\nabout schedule.
MID_EV13_039_m01_029: Yeah, but after Jula, Troy's hard to find. She leaves\nher shrine to visit the forest peoples around then.
MID_EV13_039_m01_030: We might wanna get there before she takes off so\nwe don't have to chase her down.
MID_EV13_040_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_040_m01_001: What an incredible sight. It's staggering.
MID_EV13_040_m01_002: The mountain cliffs towering above forming the\nmazelike canyons below...
MID_EV13_040_m01_003: I've heard tell of this place, but the reality has\noutstripped my imagination.
MID_EV13_040_m01_004: It's my first time too. I think I'm getting a little dizzy.
MID_EV13_040_m01_005: It really forces you to think about how vast nature is.
MID_EV13_040_m01_006: Really? Neither of you have been here before?
MID_EV13_040_m01_007: I guess if you're local to Megaira, there's not much\nreason to come.
MID_EV13_040_m01_008: This great ravine runs along the Saramis\nThoroughfare, connecting Megaira to the empire.
MID_EV13_040_m01_009: It is unlikely that the Dagdan Empire would ever\ninvade Saramis.
MID_EV13_040_m01_010: But if they did, the Tritopater Corridor would be a\nnatural fortress to hinder the enemy's advance.
MID_EV13_040_m01_011: Uh, Queen Theodora? Are we planning to go to\nwar with the empire?!
MID_EV13_040_m01_012: Don't they love us for being the Shield of Dagda?
MID_EV13_040_m01_013: I said "if," Lilian. But neither they nor we will ever\nforget Damascar.
MID_EV13_040_m01_014: A sovereign of Saramis must always face that\npossibility, however faint.
MID_EV13_040_m01_015: Once we are past here, we will be nearing\nTroy's shrine.
MID_EV13_040_m01_016: Let us hurry, Your Majesty, and hope that we make\nit before Troy's departure.
MID_EV13_040_m01_017: Halt!
MID_EV13_040_m01_018: That arrow's poisoned. It's a little different from\nthe ones I use.
MID_EV13_040_m01_019: It must be the Har Hali. There is no escaping the\nbad blood between us.
MID_EV13_040_m01_020: So you are the queen of Saramis. Our meeting here\nwas fated.
MID_EV13_040_m01_021: I am Nuzzuo, steward of the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_040_m01_022: We have claimed this land as our new stronghold.\nLeave if you value your lives.
MID_EV13_040_m01_023: Hmph. Typically, the queen would be notified of\nsuch things in advance.
MID_EV13_040_m01_024: This is an essential road for traveling to Megaira.\nIt has never belonged to you.
MID_EV13_040_m01_025: Let us refute their claim by force! Prepare for battle!
MID_EV13_041_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_041_m01_001: We are beaten, with nowhere to go. This is the end\nof the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_041_m01_002: Queen of Saramis, dispense with our souls as you\nsee fit.
MID_EV13_041_m01_003: <NCA>Ask about the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_041_m01_004: <NCB>Ask about Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_041_m01_005: <ACA>First, answer me this. Are you the current chieftain\nof the Har Hali?
MID_EV13_041_m01_006: <ACA>No. I am merely watching over them in the absence\nof our true chief.
MID_EV13_041_m01_007: <ACB>Was Bahr Vahn not your chief?
MID_EV13_041_m01_008: <ACB>After his struggle with you, Bahr Vahn was no longer\nqualified to be chief of the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_041_m01_009: <ACB>But then he got a new left hand somehow. He said\nit was one of Drake's treasures.
MID_EV13_041_m01_010: <ACB>At his command, our shaman affixed it to his wrist.
MID_EV13_041_m01_011: <ACB>So it was that Bahr Vahn found anew the strength\nrequired of a Har Hali chieftain.
MID_EV13_041_m01_012: <ACB>After that, he began behaving oddly.
MID_EV13_041_m01_013: <ACB>He grew even more cruel. Our people came to\nfear him.
MID_EV13_041_m01_014: <ACB>Craving power, Bahr Vahn left us to set out on a\nquest to become even mightier.
MID_EV13_041_m01_015: <ACB>I have been keeping our people safe in his absence.
MID_EV13_041_m01_016: As I recall, the Har Hali people called Cybele home.
MID_EV13_041_m01_017: We are a long way from there. What has happened?
MID_EV13_041_m01_018: Recently, a band of youths traveled from Dagsion\nto the land of Cybele.
MID_EV13_041_m01_019: We attempted to repel them and were defeated.\nAfterward, we led them to Balor's temple.
MID_EV13_041_m01_020: The Har Hali were defeated by children? Tell me\nmore of these youths.
MID_EV13_041_m01_021: They were led by a strong boy. There was...an eye\nin his left hand.
MID_EV13_041_m01_022: A sure sign of that boy. What business could he have\nhad there?!
MID_EV13_041_m01_023: The youths have left, but in their wake, strange\nthings have gone on in Cybele.
MID_EV13_041_m01_024: Even before, the dead walked the earth, but now\ntheir numbers have swollen.
MID_EV13_041_m01_025: Something changed when we guided the boy there.
MID_EV13_041_m01_026: Are you suggesting that the boy and his friends\nentering Balor's temple has revitalized it?
MID_EV13_041_m01_027: That'd explain why you're looking for new digs all\nthe way out here.
MID_EV13_041_m01_028: We've scuffled with these guys a bunch, but hearing\ntheir side of it, I almost feel bad for 'em.
MID_EV13_041_m01_029: Queen of Saramis. Something in you is similar to\nour chief, Bahr Vahn.
MID_EV13_041_m01_030: I do not deny it. That is why I must pass here.
MID_EV13_041_m01_031: Listen well, Nuzzuo.
MID_EV13_041_m01_032: Your chieftain is dead by my hand.
MID_EV13_041_m01_033: What?! Is this true?
MID_EV13_041_m01_034: His body was riddled with Drake's treasures. At the\nend, his mind was entirely gone.
MID_EV13_041_m01_035: He believed himself a demon god and was put\ndown accordingly.
MID_EV13_041_m01_036: I see. In a way, that is a relief to hear. We are\nfree of him now.
MID_EV13_041_m01_037: I have a proposal for you, Nuzzuo. If you seek a new\nhome, might you find one with us?
MID_EV13_041_m01_038: With the tyrant Bahr Vahn removed, there is no\nreason for Saramis not to embrace the Har Hali.
MID_EV13_041_m01_039: We share a common ancestry with the forest peoples.\nThere need be no separation between us.
MID_EV13_041_m01_040: Hm. I am grateful for the offer, Queen of Saramis.\nWe of the Har Hali will follow you from now on.
MID_EV13_042_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV13_042_m01_001: Theodora! I haven't seen you since the coup attempt.\nYou're looking well.
MID_EV13_042_m01_002: Heh. While you seem the same as ever. You have not\nchanged a bit since I was a child.
MID_EV13_042_m01_003: That's because I was created for a special purpose.\nThe years don't touch me as much.
MID_EV13_042_m01_004: I've heard about your exploits at the tournament.\nDo you have the time for a detour out here?
MID_EV13_042_m01_005: Though I've wondered how things are going with\nyour arm since I last saw you.
MID_EV13_042_m01_006: <NCA>Tell her the story.
MID_EV13_042_m01_007: <NCB>Tell her your request.
MID_EV13_042_m01_008: <ACA>At first it looked...well, mummified. But now it's\nalmost indistinguishable from my other one.
MID_EV13_042_m01_009: <ACA>It's as though it's a part of me now. And yet I feel\nincreasingly that I am part of it.
MID_EV13_042_m01_010: <ACA>What do you mean?
MID_EV13_042_m01_011: Let me be plain. I need another warding chain\nlike the one you gifted to me before.
MID_EV13_042_m01_012: What happened to it? Are you telling me it's\nalready cracked?
MID_EV13_042_m01_013: Worse. It has shattered entirely. And ever since\nthen, I have heard a strange voice.
MID_EV13_042_m01_014: In Dagsion I learned of the arm's true nature. It was\ncut from a powerful being's corpse.
MID_EV13_042_m01_015: Did you know its origin from the start?
MID_EV13_042_m01_016: Tell me! I would know who dares invade my mind.
MID_EV13_042_m01_017: This must remain between us.
MID_EV13_042_m01_018: The true origin of the arm is none other than the\ndemon god Balor, father of Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_042_m01_019: What?! Is that true?!
MID_EV13_042_m01_020: The stories of Balor say he was a vicious god.
MID_EV13_042_m01_021: For reasons unknown, he made war against the other\ngods and was killed and entombed in his temple.
MID_EV13_042_m01_022: Dagda the Great placed a secure seal on the tomb,\nwhich should have been the end of it.
MID_EV13_042_m01_023: But someone broke Dagda's seal and made off with\nthe remains.
MID_EV13_042_m01_024: This is unbelievable. Does that imply that\nDamascar's destruction was...
MID_EV13_042_m01_025: Though the temples cover it up, it must have had\nsomething to do with the breaking of the seal.
MID_EV13_042_m01_026: Then one day, the pirate Drake came to the forest\npeoples to barter with the remains.
MID_EV13_042_m01_027: Drake was originally from Damascar, so he was\non good terms with the forest peoples.
MID_EV13_042_m01_028: He must have known all along that the remains\nbelonged to Balor.
MID_EV13_042_m01_029: Now, Balor was of course the father of Yu Phas, to\nwhom the children of Damascar owed their lives.
MID_EV13_042_m01_030: But he was also an enemy of Dagda the Great. So his\nremains were hotly contested.
MID_EV13_042_m01_031: For that reason, they were divided further and\ndistributed among the forest peoples.
MID_EV13_042_m01_032: This is how Mahadu came into possession of\nBalor's right arm.
MID_EV13_042_m01_033: This is a great deal to take in, Troy.
MID_EV13_042_m01_034: Yes, Balor was a fearsome god. But he was also\nkin to Yu Phas.
MID_EV13_042_m01_035: Strange though it may sound, I am glad to have\nthis distant connection to our goddess.